>> title: Lotus Seed and Lily Bulb Soup
>> category: Soups
>> tags: pork, lotus seeds, lily bulb, red dates, cantonese, old-fire soup, stovetop
>> counters: The Soup Pot
>> aka: 蓮子百合紅棗瘦肉湯, lin zi baak hap hung zou sau juk tong, lin ji bak hap hung jou sau yuk tong, lotus seed and lily bulb soup, lotus seed lily bulb and red date pork soup, 老火湯, lo fo tong
>> servings: 4
>> time: 3 hr
>> slack: forgiving — nothing in this pot has a clock on it; what a household decides before it goes on is the red dates, which are pitted because a pot made with the stones in is held to turn 燥, and that is not a thing you can take back out at hour two
>> step.1: The 安神 pot — calm and sleep is the tradition's own reason for it — and the one made in a house where somebody has not been sleeping. Lotus seed and lily bulb are the pair that carries it; the pork is only there to give the water a body.
>> step.2: blanch from cold, then rinse the pork
>> step.3: soak the seeds and the lily 30 min
>> step.4: simmer 2 1/2 hr, barely a quiver
>> step.5: season at the end, never at the start
>> step.6: The broth is the dish. The solids — 湯渣, tong zaa — are spent by the end; they go on a side plate with soy sauce, or they do not.

The 安神 pot — calm and sleep is the tradition's own reason for it — and the one made in a house where somebody has not been sleeping. Lotus seed and lily bulb are the pair that carries it; the pork is only there to give the water a body.

Blanch @lean pork{1%lb}(450 g; sau juk, in two whole pieces) from cold in @water{2%qt}(1.9 L) in a #soup pot{}, ~blanch{8%min} up to a rolling boil, then pour the whole lot away, rinse the pork under the tap and scrub the pot out.

Soak @lotus seeds{1/2%cup}(lin zi; push the bitter green core out of each one, or the whole pot goes bitter), @dried lily bulb{1/3%cup}(baak hap; petal-shaped scales — for the lungs, and the same 安神) and @red dates{6}(hung zou; pitted) in cold water, ~soak{30%min}, then lift them out and leave the grit behind.

Simmer @&(~2)blanched pork{} with @&(~1)soaked seeds and lily{} and @cold water{2 1/2%qt}(2.4 L; the pot is filled once and not topped up) in the rinsed #soup pot{}, lid ajar, ~simmer{2 1/2%hr} at a bare quiver, unstirred.

Season @&(~1)soup{} with @kosher salt{3/4%tsp}, at the end and never at the start.

The broth is the dish. The solids — 湯渣, tong zaa — are spent by the end; they go on a side plate with soy sauce, or they do not.
